      "original_context": {
        "full_target": "Let \\(p\\) be any prime, \\(K\\) any field of characteristic \\(p\\), and\n\\(\\lambda\\) an integer with \\(0\\leq\\lambda<p\\).\nLet \\(V(\\lambda)\\) be the complex irreducible highest-weight\n\\(\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)\\)-module of highest weight \\(\\lambda\\),\nof dimension \\(\\lambda+1\\). Its Chevalley generators satisfy\n\n\\[\n[h,x]=2x,\\qquad[h,y]=-2y,\\qquad[x,y]=h.\n\\]\n\nChoose a nonzero highest-weight vector \\(v\\) with \\(xv=0\\) and\n\\(hv=\\lambda v\\). Let \\(U_{\\mathbb Z}\\) be the integer subalgebra of\nthe universal enveloping algebra generated by all divided powers\n\\(X_r=x^r/r!\\), \\(Y_r=y^r/r!\\), for integers \\(r\\geq0\\).\nAn **admissible lattice** \\(M\\subset V(\\lambda)\\) is a free abelian\nsubgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis, stable under\n\\(U_{\\mathbb Z}\\). It is arbitrary, not necessarily the minimal lattice.\n\nPut \\(V(K)=M\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}K\\). The Lie algebra\n\\(L(K)=(\\mathbb Zx+\\mathbb Zy+\\mathbb Zh)\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}K\\)\nacts by the induced lattice operators. This is the Chevalley\n\\(\\mathfrak{sl}_2\\) construction also in characteristic 2.\nProve that \\(V(K)\\) is nonzero and every \\(K\\)-linear subspace\ninvariant under \\(x,y,h\\) is zero or all of \\(V(K)\\).\nBoth \\(\\lambda=0\\) and \\(p=2\\) are included; \\(K\\) need not be\nalgebraically closed.",
        "hypotheses": [
          {
            "id": "H001",
            "statement": "p is prime.",
            "origin": "problem.md:16"
          },
          {
            "id": "H002",
            "statement": "K has characteristic p.",
            "origin": "problem.md:16"
          },
          {
            "id": "H003",
            "statement": "0≤λ<p, with λ an integer.",
            "origin": "problem.md:17"
          },
          {
            "id": "H004",
            "statement": "V=V(λ) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(ℂ)-module of highest weight λ and complex dimension λ+1.",
            "origin": "problem.md:18-20"
          },
          {
            "id": "H005",
            "statement": "The complex-linear Chevalley operators satisfy hx−xh=2x, hy−yh=−2y, xy−yx=h; v≠0, xv=0, hv=λv.",
            "origin": "problem.md:20-27"
          },
          {
            "id": "H006",
            "statement": "M⊂V is an arbitrary admissible lattice: it is a free abelian subgroup possessing an integer basis which is also a complex basis of V, and it is stable under U_Z (equivalently under every X_r,Y_r for r≥0). M is not assumed minimal.",
            "origin": "problem.md:27-32"
          }
        ],
        "conclusion": "U=V(K)=M⊗_ℤ K is nonzero, and every K-linear subspace W⊂U invariant under the induced x,y,h actions equals zero or U; equivalently U is irreducible for the prescribed L_K action. Both λ=0 and p=2 are included, and K need not be algebraically closed."
      },
